Each depositor insured to at least $250,000 per insured bank Attn: Accounting Department Herewith we would like to notify you about the latest alterations in the FDIC insurance coverage. During the period from 12-31-2010 to 12-31-2012 all assets in a ""interest-bearing transaction account"" are provided with an unlimited coverage by the FDIC. Please note, that this coverage is temporary and besides the FDIC's common deposit insurance regulations. The term ""interest-bearing transaction account"" means a traditional checking account or demand deposit account on which no interest is paid by the insured depository institution. For more details about this temporary FDIC unlimited coverage, please enter http://www.fdic.gov/. Yours faithfully, Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation.",d02,Shopping and Retail,"GENERAL SETTINGS
